📗
  🏰 Which proxies in front of the server are its own, as
  server.trustedProxies says it: a number of them, or their addresses and
  networks.

  A number means that whoever connects is believed, that many entries deep
  into the X-Forwarded- headers. A list (10.0.0.0/8, 192.168.1.5, ::1) means
  that a request's forwarded headers are read only when it connected from an
  address in the list, and then as far as the entries of X-Forwarded-For,
  read from the right, are in the list themselves: the first that is not is
  the client. An IPv4 address that a socket gives as ::ffff:10.0.0.1 is that
  IPv4 address, and the zone an address may carry (%eth0) is left out.
