  📗
    How many entries of the X-Forwarded- headers, from the right, are
    believed for a request that connected from *peer* and came with
    *forwarded* as its X-Forwarded-For. *reads* says whether that header is
    one the proxies write. With a number that is the number, whoever
    connected. With a list it is 0 for a peer that is not in it, and
    otherwise as many entries as were written by the listed: the entries are
    read from the right up to the first address that is not listed, which is
    the client, and at least one is believed, since a listed proxy passed the
    request on.
